        "title": {
          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Raju used a compass to draw a circle with the centre on his notebook.\n\"The distance from the centre is always the same,\" he said."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "radius",
          "diameter",
          "compass"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A compass draws a circle. Place the point on the centre and the pencil at the radius. The radius is the distance from the centre to the circle and the diameter is twice the radius.\nTo copy a line segment, set the compass to its length and mark the same length elsewhere.\nA ruler and compass can draw many shapes accurately."
        }
      },
